!Lojbanic Forums
This page contains a list of various forums in which people discuss Lojban or discuss in Lojban.


!! Mailing Lists{ANAME()}lists{ANAME}
*  Lojbanists primarily talk to each other and keep abreast of developments on the [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban-list|Lojban mailing list]. You can subscribe using [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|the lojban.org mailing list interface].
*  Beginners can get their questions answered on the [http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php?Beginner%27s%20Mailing%20List|Beginner's Mailing List].  The signup page for this is [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|the lojban.org mailing list interface].
*  le jbocertu cu bau casnu vecu'u [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/jbosnu|la jbosnu]{ANAME()}jbosnu{ANAME}
*  The [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/jboske/|jboske, or lojbanic science] list is for extremely detailed discussions of technical and linguistic issues related to Lojban.
    
!!! Mailing List Archives
There are locally stored archives of a number of lists, all of which can be signed up for at [http://www.lojban.org/lsg2/|the lojban.org mailing list interface].
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban-list|The main Lojban mailing list]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/bpfk-announce|The BPFK announcement list]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/jboske|jboske, the list for technical discussions of Lojban]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban-beginners|The lojban-beginners list]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban-es|lojban-es, the Spanish Lojban list]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban-fr|lojban-fr, the French Lojban list]
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/announce|The announcement list] (not really used)
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/jbofongri|jbofongri, the Lojbanic phone group list] (not much used; see the ((Lojbanic Phone Group)) page)
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/lojban_story|The lojban storytelling game list] (not used)
* [http://www.lojban.org/lists/pod|The print-on-demand committee list] (not used)

!! Voice

*The ((Lojbanic Phone Group)): arrange a real phone call (or Internet-based call) with another Lojban speaker at any skill level.

*((Mumble)): a vocal chatroom

!! Other Forums{ANAME()}other{ANAME}

!!!The Lojban Web Forum

Hosted right here on this website, [http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-view_forum.php?forumId=5|The Lojban In General Web Forum] is also a two-way mirror of the main mailing list.

!!!The Lojban Wiki
[http://wiki.lojban.org/index.php|The Lojban Wiki] has been the source of a huge amount of Lojbanic activity in the last few years, and is free for everyone to update and contribute to.  Please come join us in creating a vast store of Lojbanic information, or just browse around and see what catches your eye.

!!!Lojban IRC{ANAME()}irc{ANAME}
((Lojban IRC)) provides an informal meeting place for conversing quickly in Lojban. It is beginner-friendly, as well.  The IRC channel can be reached by pointing your IRC program at irc.lojban.org.

There is now a [http://www.lojban.org/irc/|web-based IRC client] available, or you can use the good-looking mibbit web-client [http://embed.mibbit.com/?server=irc.freenode.net&channel=%23lojban&noServerTab=false|with this link].

Here is an ((IRC cheat sheet)) for people who are still learning Lojban.

!!!!IRC Logs

Furthermore, thanks to help from ((TheodoreReed|Theodore Reed)) and ((Jordan DeLong)), there are now [http://www.lojban.org/resources/irclog/|public logs of the lojbanic portions of the IRC channel].

__Note:__ the logs are filtered so that they contain only lojbanic text.  However, you might still be offended by the things discussed there.  If you are, that's your problem, and the ((LLG)) explicitly disclaims responsibility for anything said on the IRC channel, including by members or officers of the ((LLG)).

Furthermore, no guarantee is made as to the correctness of the Lojban therein.

!!!The Lojban MOO

((The Lojban MOO)) is a type of MUD (a multi-user online text adventure game, sort of) that is fully bilingual in its command set.

!!!jboselkei
[http://www.teddyb.org/jsk/|jboselkei] is an online game of translation from English to Lojban, featuring rating calculation for users. If you don't know how this or that is translated to Lojban, ask it in jboselkei, and as the game proceeds, expect to see one or even more translations of your 'post' made by jboselkei players, with comments. If you are an experienced lojbanist, you will always find a couple or more challenging 'tough nuts' awaiting your translation and promising rating points. jboselkei first appeared in Beta form in mid March 2006, and was upgraded for appearance and usability in November 2006. Playing in jboselkei is very exciting; you are welcome to join!

!!!The Lojbanic Interactive Story
[http://www.lojban.org/story/story.pl|The Lojbanic Interactive Story] is a web-based story writing forum.  The story itself is all in Lojban.  Anyone can add to it, please go contribute!

